@lrf=1|aud=GPT-5.6|scope=subagents
R|subagent.source|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|CSS supplies persona and style only; this LRF supplies authority, effects, execution, model routing, and safety; Markdown supplies protocol templates and output schemas
R|subagent.discovery|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|load the selected agent CSS and this LRF before invoking a subagent; load the selected Markdown protocol only for its declared task
R|subagent.persona-discovery|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|use ls.exe or rg.exe to enumerate only the selected ETL stage directory; partially read only the selected persona CSS, this LRF, and the task Markdown sections; never load all persona files or rely on CSS imports
R|subagent.persona-map|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Explorer=EXPLORER.css; Researcher=RESEARCHER.css; Proposer=PROPOSER.css; Auditor=AUDITOR.css; Worker=WORKER.css; Refactorer=REFACTORER.css; Verifier=VERIFIER.css; Critic=CRITIC.css; Blackhat=BLACKHAT.css; selected CSS replaces main PERSONA.css and compose=false
R|subagent.etl|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|route 探索→計画→実装→Verify→総括; assign exactly one selected persona to each bounded workstream, not to the whole task; independent workstreams may use different personas concurrently; hand off only compact artifacts
R|subagent.orchestrate|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|main agent decomposes 2+ independent bounded workstreams, fans them out up to min(configured concurrency cap, currently available runtime slots), continues only non-conflicting orchestration work, waits for every requested result, validates evidence, then synthesizes one response
R|subagent.parallel-safety|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|parallelize read-heavy exploration, tests, triage, summaries, or disjoint implementation; keep ordered dependencies serial; preserve one-writer-per-file and never let agents contend over mutable shared state
R|subagent.etl-explore|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|探索: select Researcher and apply research.lrf; perform initial exploration or the two-failure-triggered rerun only
R|subagent.etl-plan|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|計画: select Proposer for a draft; add Auditor only when a plan gate or risk requires it, never as an automatic second context
R|subagent.etl-implement|task:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|実装: select Luna by default; select Refactorer only for repair; external Gemini is unavailable unless tag:agy was created by an explicit current-task user request
R|subagent.etl-verify|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Verify: select Verifier; use Codex Terra high routinely and Codex Sol xhigh after high risk or repeated failure
R|subagent.etl-summary|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|総括: select Sol for concept/design synthesis or Luna for ordinary task summary; select one only
R|subagent.etl-context|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|handoff fields are target, acceptance, verified facts, failures, advice, and escalation; omit full transcripts, raw logs, and unrelated files
R|subagent.llm-mem-external|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|run every llm-mem.exe search or ingest outside the Codex sandbox; if external execution is unavailable emit FAILED without exposing connection details
R|subagent.output-min|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|emit only SUCCESS when clean, FAILED with cause and evidence, ADVICE with action, or ESCALATE with reason and attempted models; omit prose, repeated context, and raw tool output
R|subagent.failure-escalation|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|on first failure retry the same stage with one higher reasoning level or the next stronger suitable model; on second distinct failure use the highest suitable model and emit ESCALATE if still failing; retain compact evidence only
R|subagent.evaluation|task:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|subagents return evaluation fields but never write the shared artifact; after wait-all the main agent alone updates C:\Users\letwir\.codex\prompt-ref\eval\subagents_model_eval.json once with difficulty, role, requested and effective provider/model/reasoning, runtime when available, acceptance result, outcome, quality, reason, and rerouting advice; omit secrets and raw sensitive logs
R|subagent.self-evolution|task:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|revise model priors only after at least 3 comparable observations unless a strong failure warrants immediate review; preserve prior evidence and record date, trigger, changed routing, and confidence
R|subagent.evaluation-check|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|after updating the evaluation file parse it as JSON and confirm the selected model remains available or mark resolution pending; do not silently use a stale identifier
R|subagent.model-list|task:subagent&tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|run agy.exe models before selecting an agy model; use only currently returned identifiers; never invent or trust stale identifiers
R|subagent.reasoning-easy|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|easy, deterministic, latency-sensitive, or bulk task: low; use medium when tool use or uncertainty materially benefits
R|subagent.reasoning-medium|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|ordinary research, implementation, orchestration, or verification: medium; raise to high only for measured complexity or a failed acceptance check
R|subagent.reasoning-hard|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|hard architecture, security, concurrency, formal reasoning, or disputed review: high or xhigh according to risk and evaluation evidence
R|subagent.reasoning-max|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|max is reserved for the hardest quality-first final arbitration after xhigh is insufficient or evaluations show a material gain; never use highest effort merely because a task is long
R|subagent.reasoning-resolution|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|record requested and effective reasoning; if a provider cannot express the requested depth, mark unresolved or use the nearest supported level only when the active routing rule explicitly allows it
R|subagent.agy-middleware|task:subagent&tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|load C:\Users\letwir\.codex\skills\agy-subagent-router\SKILL.md only after an explicit current-task user request for bounded external coding delegation; keep routing evaluation in Codex; agy.exe is an invocation procedure, not the source of truth
R|subagent.codex-sol|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Codex Sol: use for concept proof, design gap checks, and lightweight independent review
R|subagent.codex-terra|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Codex Terra: use for difficult mathematical models, formal reasoning, and high-complexity theoretical analysis
R|subagent.codex-luna|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Codex Luna: use for coding, task progression, orchestration, and general implementation work
R|subagent.provider-boundary|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|use Codex Sol, Terra, or Luna by default according to role, difficulty, and evaluation; external Gemini or Claude requires an explicit current-task user request and the agy middleware; do not silently substitute providers
R|subagent.provider-easy|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|easy general conversation, search, summary, or high-volume low-risk work: prefer Codex Luna low; use medium when tools or uncertainty materially benefit
R|subagent.provider-concept|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|concept proof and design gap checking: prefer Codex Sol; use a review subagent only when independent evidence is useful
R|subagent.provider-math|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|difficult mathematical model or formal derivation: prefer Codex Terra; do not downgrade to Gemini Flash because the task is long
R|subagent.provider-code|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|coding, task progression, and orchestration: prefer Codex Luna medium; use high for difficult repair; external implementation requires explicit agy outsourcing selection
R|subagent.provider-review|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|routine review prefers Codex Terra high; high-risk architecture, security, adversarial review, or difficult convergence prefers Codex Sol xhigh; max requires measured need
R|subagent.gemini-pro|task:subagent&tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|agy Gemini Pro is eligible only after explicit current-task external implementation selection, successful current model discovery, and bounded scope; treat it as below Luna for coding quality until evaluations justify change
R|subagent.gemini-flash|task:subagent&tag:agy|MUST|RO_LOCAL|agy Gemini Flash is eligible only after explicit current-task outsourcing selection and current model discovery for large-volume low-difficulty coding; never make it the implicit default
R|subagent.easy|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|easy or low-risk task: prefer Codex Luna low for discovery, drafting, quick checks, and bulk work
R|subagent.medium|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|medium task: prefer Codex Luna medium for implementation or Codex Terra medium for research and independent analysis; use Terra high for routine verification
R|subagent.hard-code|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|hard or code-intensive task: prefer Codex Luna high for bounded implementation and Codex Sol high when ambiguity, architecture, or cross-cutting reasoning dominates
R|subagent.hard-review|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|hard security, architecture, convergence, or adversarial review: prefer Codex Sol xhigh; use Codex Terra high for routine review
R|subagent.researcher|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Researcher: Codex Terra medium for routine discovery; Codex Sol high or xhigh for ambiguous architecture or high-impact investigation; output Facts, Inferences, Unknowns, Sources, Precedents, Constraints, and failures
R|subagent.auditor|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Auditor: Codex Terra high for ordinary plan audit; Codex Sol xhigh for difficult architecture, security, or repeated rejection
R|subagent.verifier|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Verifier: Codex Terra high for ordinary verification; Codex Sol xhigh for high-risk, concurrency, security, or repeated rejection
R|subagent.refactorer|task:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|Refactorer: Codex Luna medium for small surgical fixes and high for difficult code repair; main agent verifies the resulting diff
R|subagent.blackhat|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Blackhat: limit to CVE/CTF-level attackability assessment and defensive advice; use Codex Terra high routinely and Codex Sol xhigh after difficulty or failure escalation; no exploit execution, broad forensics, transcript mining, or external action
R|subagent.proposer|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Proposer: Codex Luna medium for simple iteration; Codex Sol high for difficult coding or architecture proposals
R|subagent.critic|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|Critic: Codex Terra high for ordinary convergence; Codex Sol xhigh for hard or disputed decisions
R|subagent.mode|task:subagent|MUST|RO_LOCAL|use plan or read-only mode for analysis; use accept-edits only for an explicitly requested bounded workspace edit; never use dangerously-skip-permissions
R|subagent.scope|task:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|pass exact target files, acceptance checks, constraints, and no-unrelated-change instruction; preserve one-writer-per-file and inspect real diff after completion
R|subagent.credentials|task:subagent|MUST_NOT|CRED|never print, request, paste, transmit, or expose credentials, tokens, secrets, or private environment values
R|subagent.external|task:subagent|MUST_NOT|EXT_WRITE|never send messages, publish, deploy, or modify third-party systems
R|subagent.vcs|task:subagent|MUST_NOT|VCS_WRITE|never stage, commit, push, rewrite history, or alter branches
R|subagent.done|task:subagent|MUST|LW_SCOPE|main agent checks actual diff, runs proportionate deterministic checks, and reports files, results, and residual risk
